  "body": "Bind Robert's trip status, sharing and demo-session routes and preserve the updated owner reads' server timestamps. This candidate follows PR74 at 4c138ca1d00742400a850cd72b0888cc59260a36 and PR65 at 3ea6e1b06e6dc3d3d01360f28ae9c61751657830. It keeps server check, incident and delivery facts, explicit arrival and contact-role inputs, scoped location absence, source age and server readAt distinct. No monitoring projection, row clock or stronger snapshot guarantee is added.\n\nCandidate head: 75bdffa42d858c82a8dcb0af11bc78803e3d9a09. Stacked on accepted PR59 / 7e241c39a31d4eaba5f8028fd977e06f6ca72d4d; that branch and its acceptance remain unchanged. Only lane45 API, tests and boundary documentation change.\n\nThe latest narrow correction addresses Q52's actual contact UI review finding: a 401 clears credentials and protected data, but a queued binding callback can reopen the disposed view as verifying after gateway sign-out. Retire session notifications after binding disposal while preserving its final synchronous clear. Both a reentrant helper regression and the actual frozen contact view store at e2c1e677cf3ec3fa9c7f91529b082ab5b8ff91e6 reproduce verifying before the fix and pass afterward. Both contact and driver views remain closed and recover through explicit gateway begin. Feature source remains unchanged. This is existing-PR remediation under the review-only freeze.\n\nSharing requires the original caller key/body and one HTTP attempt. Lost responses remain unknown. The five owner reads require the root readAt supplied by the server handler clock before its read transaction. Missing or malformed timestamps fail closed; nested bootstrap entries receive no invented clocks. Read-committed statements may observe changes between statements; bootstrap is not a repeatable-read snapshot.\n\nDemo creation requires explicit demo:true and sends one anonymous POST with an empty object, no bearer/cookies or idempotency key, following the server's actorless exception. The token-bearing world is for a trusted in-memory demo host. createDemoSessionGateway fixes demo mode and requires an explicit persona; each explicit begin creates a fresh world, retains only that persona's active credential and awaits actual typed /v1/me with a matching server UUID. Parsed JWT claims supply metadata and expiry only. End/dispose retire old acquisitions without retry, persistence or production-OIDC fallback. A host coordinating personas in the same world must explicitly manage the sensitive SDK result in memory; the fixed-persona helper does not cache worlds.\n\nValidation on the current source with Node24.17.0, existing read-only TypeScript5.9.3 and locked dependencies, without installs:\n\n- 91 native and frozen-view checks passed, including wire shapes, ambiguity, malformed timestamps, anonymous demo acquisition, all personas, late acquisition and the two new disposal regressions.\n- 16 pinned contact/driver checks plus three frozen-foundation compile checks passed (19 combined).\n- Seven real signed HTTP/PostgreSQL checks passed using exact PR74 source plus only PR65's frozen read module in a temporary test archive. They cover persona authentication, source readAt clocks, arrival, committed-but-lost sharing, same-key reconciliation with one SQL event, changed-body409, stale location, active SOS after arrival, revoked-contact403, mutual issuer401 rejection, and clearing session/gateway/bound context on actual verifier refusal. Owned temporary resources are cleaned up; no provider or worker runs.\n- Strict TypeScript passed in NodeNext and ESNext/Bundler; whitespace clean. Both new regressions failed with verifying instead of closed before the helper correction.\n\nReproduction is in docs/client/api-boundary.md. The view regression requires the fetched frozen contact object and uses synthetic HTTP with native store assertions; it is not browser acceptance. Real-backend tests require fetched source pins, Q46's disposable-resource helper at c2501a4, explicit existing dependencies/compiler and an owned PostgreSQL binary/port. They reject a shared admin URL and never read an application .env. The route mount is test-only.\n\nQ47 independently accepted the previous 2860d8593f90e1a327ac86cee0ef313d94692489 head in https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/pull/81#pullrequestreview-5560759013 . That acceptance does not cover this new binding delta. Current-head independent review, Q52's targeted UI confirmation and Q43 auth/privacy review remain pending before adoption. Backend policy findings remain separate; Q44 alone integrates. No new feature work or composition is authorized by this correction.\n\nThis candidate supplies no recipient discovery, automatic polling/deadline policy, configured check timings, real provider login, live sends or full-app/device acceptance. Optional consented-phone live-demo configuration is not enabled by this client or its tests. Earlier c250/3283 browser evidence stays pinned to that older fixture and acquisition path.\n\nRefs #14, #16, #22, #29\n",
